accel/tcg: remember where I/O split a TB, and translate it that short

An MMIO access that is not the last insn of its TB triggers
cpu_io_recompile: longjmp out, find the TB by host pc, unwind, and run the
access alone in a 1-insn CF_NOIRQ TB. The original TB stays cached, so a
guest that polls a device register in a loop pays all of that on every
iteration. The Octatrack firmware's DSP status polls did it ~880k times a
second.

Record, per TB start pc, how many insns reach the access, invalidate the TB,
and cap its retranslation there so the access is the TB's last insn and
can_do_io holds. Interrupt behaviour is unchanged: nothing can be taken
between the prefix and the access in either version, and the TB ends after
the access in both.

Side effect: guest-instruction budgets (0012) now count exactly. The split
path charged the whole original TB for a prefix, then the suffix again, and
left the access itself uncounted.

Measured: unthrottled capacity ~100% -> ~117% of real time, paced 94.4% ->
98.5% including boot. test-emac 18/18, test-emu-audio 3/3 clean, 72/72
verified trig taps first time.

